<p>A product retailer has manuals that customers and support staff must search for answers. We will deploy an assistant that answers questions from those manuals.</p>
<h2 id="customer-benefit">Customer benefit</h2>
<p>The goal is less time searching documents and fewer repetitive support questions. Answers include the supporting manual passages, so users can check specifications and instructions. When the manuals cannot answer a question, the assistant says so.</p>
<p><strong>Example:</strong> “Does the Harbor Travel Kettle work on 110 V?” The assistant points to the manual's 220–240 V requirement rather than guessing.</p>
<h2 id="what-we-will-do">What we will do</h2>
<ol><li>Deploy the supplied Java and Python applications and their Azure services.</li><li>Upload fictional product manuals and watch them become searchable.</li><li>Ask product questions, inspect cited answers and test an unsupported question.</li><li>Inspect the running services, run the deployment smoke test and clean up.</li></ol>
<p>All application code is supplied. Your work is mainly to build, configure, deploy and inspect it.</p>
<h2 id="what-you-will-learn">What you will learn</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Containers:</strong> build, tag and push Docker images; deploy and inspect AKS Pods, Services, probes, logs and rollouts.</li><li><strong>Events:</strong> connect Blob uploads through Event Grid to a small Python Function; distinguish notifications from queued work.</li><li><strong>Data and RAG:</strong> apply Flyway migrations, chunk manuals, create embeddings and retrieve filtered evidence with PostgreSQL/pgvector.</li><li><strong>Asynchronous chat:</strong> use Service Bus request/reply, persistent state, correlation IDs and retry-safe processing.</li><li><strong>Identity and configuration:</strong> use managed/workload identity, Key Vault secrets and App Configuration settings.</li><li><strong>Operations:</strong> read logs, diagnose failures and verify the deployment and cleanup.</li></ul>
<h2 id="before-you-start">Before you start</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Azure:</strong> an active subscription, resource/role-assignment permissions, and model/VM quota.</li><li><strong>Local:</strong> Azure CLI, Bicep, Docker, kubectl, Java 21, Python 3.12+ and Git. On Windows, use Ubuntu in WSL2 with Docker Desktop integration.</li></ul>
<p>Use the <a href="./prerequisites.html#before-you-begin">prerequisite checklist</a> and <a href="./prerequisites.html#windows-setup">setup downloads</a>. Allow about 3½ hours <em>after</em> setup; this estimate has not been timed.</p>
<details class="optional" id="finished"><summary>Applications and source code</summary>
<table><thead><tr><th>Application / source repo</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>{{repo:products}}</td><td>Java 21 / Spring Boot on AKS. Server-rendered upload/chat UI; JDBC, PostgreSQL and Flyway. Always at least one replica.</td></tr><tr><td>{{repo:embedder}}</td><td>Python Function. Reads uploaded manuals, creates chunks/embeddings and stores them in pgvector.</td></tr><tr><td>{{repo:chat}}</td><td>Python worker on AKS. Retrieves chunks, calls the chat model and replies through Service Bus. Runs as one worker replica.</td></tr></tbody></table>
</details>
<details class="optional" id="upload-flow"><summary>Upload and indexing flow</summary>
<figure class="flow" aria-label="Upload and indexing architecture"><div class="flow-node"><strong>Products</strong>Commit product + manual ID</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Private blob</strong>Upload .txt</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Event Grid → Function</strong>Read, chunk, embed</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>PostgreSQL</strong>Store vectors; mark ready</div><figcaption>Upload success precedes indexing completion. Event Grid carries a notification; the Function reads the blob separately.</figcaption></figure>
</details>
<details class="optional" id="question-flow"><summary>Question and answer flow</summary>
<figure class="flow" aria-label="Asynchronous RAG architecture"><div class="flow-node"><strong>Products + DB</strong>Persist question + outbox</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Request queue</strong>Service Bus</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Chat worker</strong>Embed → retrieve → generate</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Reply queue → Products</strong>Persist answer; browser polls</div><figcaption>Persistent request/correlation IDs connect the flow. Embeddings find evidence; the LLM generates the answer.</figcaption></figure>
</details>
